        return False
    for I in range(2, int(n**0.5)+1):
        if n % I == 0:
            return False
    return True

This function takes an integer n as input and returns True if n is prime, and False otherwise. It first checks if n is less than or equal to 1, which are not prime numbers. Then, it loops through all integers from 2 to the square root of n (rounded up) and checks if n is divisible by any of them. If n is divisible by any of these numbers, it is not prime, so the function returns False. If n is not divisible by any of these numbers, it is prime, so the function returns True.```

