public boolean isPowerOfThree(int n) {
    if (n <= 0) {
        return false;
    }
    int x = 0;
    while (n > 1) {
        n /= 3;
        x++;
    }
    return n == 1;
}
```

This solution uses a while loop to repeatedly divide n by 3 until n becomes 1. The number of times n is divided by 3 is stored in x. If n becomes 1, then x is the exponent of 3 that satisfies n == 3^x. Otherwise, n is not a power of three.

To solve the problem without loops or recursion, we can use the fact that 3^x is always a multiple of 9 for any integer x. We can check if n is a multiple of 9 by checking if n % 9 == 0. If it is, then n is a power of three. If it is not, then n is not a power of three.

